{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"I fixed a stuck consumer and submitted the mitigation. The submission returned a 200. I haven't checked end-user latency or request success. I also didn't investigate the frontend's `ECONNREFUSED` error from 05:16:48, which was probably a startup race.\n\n**Cause:** The `orders-validator` consumer stopped at offset 20 of the `orders-fulfillment` topic. That record wasn't valid JSON, and the consumer's code paused on any record that failed validation. Every order after it was never processed, even though `order-stream` kept producing them.\n\n**Fix:** I edited `consumer.py` in the `orders-pipeline-scripts` ConfigMap. The consumer now logs a malformed record, commits its offset and moves on. I restarted `orders-validator`. It is now processing new orders again (it was at offset 48 when I last looked), and all pods are Running.\n\nThe malformed record is skipped and not saved anywhere, so it can't be recovered or inspected later. The ConfigMap edit is also live-only. If it's managed from a manifest elsewhere, that source needs the same change."}}
